# Architecture

@@TITLE_EN@@ — @@TITLE_AR@@

## Components

| Component | Path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Entity model | `app/model.py`, `app/schema.json` | Entity definitions as data; record validation |
| Storage | `app/db.py`, `migrations/` | SQLite connection, versioned up/down migrations, parameterized CRUD, scoping |
| Accounts | `app/auth.py` | PBKDF2 passwords, sessions, CSRF tokens, sign-in lockout |
| HTTP server | `app/server.py` | JSON REST API, static files, security headers, request guards |
| Seed | `app/seed.py`, `app/seed_data.json` | Synthetic sample records |
| Frontend | `static/` | Bilingual accessible UI (vanilla JS, no build step) |
| Command line | `manage.py`, `app/__main__.py` | serve, migrate, seed, create-account, test |
| Tests | `tests/` | Unit, API integration, acceptance, browser E2E |

## Decisions

### ADR-001 Modular monolith on the Python standard library
- Context: the specification asks for runtime `python3-stdlib` and database `sqlite`,
  no paid services, and independence from the hub.
- Decision: one process (`http.server` + `sqlite3`), entity model as data.
- Trade-offs: no third-party framework to patch or license-review; a threaded
  stdlib server suits a single team or local use, not high concurrency.
- Revisit when: measured load exceeds a single process, or multi-tenant hosting is required.

### ADR-002 Same-origin JSON API with per-session CSRF tokens
- Writes require `application/json`, a same-origin request and the session's `X-CSRF-Token`;
  no CORS is offered.
- Revisit when: a separate frontend origin or third-party API clients are required.

### ADR-003 Local accounts, cookie sessions, roles from the specification
- Accounts are local (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, per-account salt); sessions are random tokens in
  an `HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict` cookie; every API route checks the role permission for its
  method (roles: @@ROLES@@).
- Revisit when: the owner selects an identity provider, or needs password reset/MFA (open item OI-IDENTITY).

### ADR-004 Bilingual UI without a build step
- Arabic (RTL) and English (LTR) strings live in `static/i18n.json`; the server renders
  `lang`/`dir` for `/?lang=<locale>`; CSS uses logical properties so one stylesheet serves
  both directions; dates are stored as ISO-8601 and displayed with `Intl.DateTimeFormat`.

### ADR-005 Acceptance criteria as executable tests
- Each criterion of the specification (`METHOD /path [condition] returns NNN [and …]`) is
  stored in `app/acceptance.json` and executed by `tests/test_acceptance.py`.
